root-daynight
=============

root-daynight is a small X11 helper that switches the root window
background between day and night modes based on local time.

The script always applies a solid background color using xsetroot.
Wallpaper support is optional and applied on top of the color.

It is intended for traditional X11 window manager setups.


Configuration
-------------

All settings are defined inside the script.

DAY_COLOR / NIGHT_COLOR
    Solid root background colors.

DAY_WALLPAPER / NIGHT_WALLPAPER
    Optional wallpapers. Leave empty to disable.

DAY_START / NIGHT_START
    Hours (0–23) when day and night modes start.

SLEEP_TIME
    Time in seconds between checks.


Dependencies
------------

- X11
- xsetroot
- feh (only required if wallpapers are used)


Usage
-----

Make the script executable and start it from your X session:

    chmod +x root-daynight.sh
    ./root-daynight.sh &


Notes
-----

The script is X11-only. Wayland is not supported.

